WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.210
Roles and access in ONEMS.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.720
What each person sees, and what they can
do,

3
00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.590
depends on their roles in their country's
account.

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.090
Here is how it works.

5
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.630
Every account has the same six roles.

6
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.770
The Account Manager heads the account and
decides the team's access.

7
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.510
The Allocation Plan Manager prepares the
shipment plans.

8
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:28.410
The Panelist Manager looks after the
panelists, their incidents and their
availability.

9
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.550
The Materials Supplier manages materials.

10
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.330
The DO coordinator handles the RFID side.

11
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.090
And the UPU account manager follows the
account for the UPU.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.610
For each menu option, a role gives one of
three rights.

13
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.930
Edit: you see the screen and you can
change data.

14
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.000
View: you see the screen, but the create,
save

15
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.370
and delete buttons are hidden, and a View
only badge appears.

16
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.050
Or no access: the option does not appear
in the menu.

17
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.730
If you have several roles, the highest
right wins.

18
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.780
For example, the Panelist Manager has View
on Stock Management,

19
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.220
and the Materials Supplier has Edit.

20
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.770
With both roles, you have Edit.

21
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:16.350
And a user with no role only sees the
reporting screens and the Help centre.

22
00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:23.210
If a menu option is missing, or you need
Edit where you only have View,

23
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.730
ask the Account Manager or the UPU account
manager of your account.

24
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.410
Only they can change its roles and rights.

25
00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:32.540
The change is saved at once.

26
00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.170
Reload the page to see your updated menu.

27
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:40.540
Account Managers and UPU account managers
use the tab

28
00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.090
Administration, Roles and access.

29
00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.110
In Account contacts, type the emails that
receive the automatic notices.

30
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.490
A contact does not give access to ONEMS.

31
00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.390
In Rights of each role, choose Edit, View
or no access for each menu option.

32
00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.250
There is no save button:

33
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.010
the change is saved at once.

34
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:05.950
In Users and their roles, tick or untick a
role for each user.

35
00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.880
Review any role marked Provisional:

36
00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:12.150
confirm it, or replace it with the right
one.

37
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.710
Back to template undoes all changes to the
rights.

38
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.630
And Latest changes shows who changed what,
and when.

39
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.130
Each account keeps its own rights,
contacts and roles.

40
00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:28.130
A change in yours does not affect other
countries.

41
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.350
For the full guide, open Roles and access
in the Help centre.
